Give a server built without bus enumeration libdrm's compiler flags.

configure adds LIBDRM_CFLAGS/LIBDRM_LIBS to the Xorg flags in one place only:
inside the branch that configures libpciaccess.  The assumption is that a
server which talks to a display manager also enumerates the PCI bus, and on
every system upstream builds for it that holds.

This server is built --disable-pciaccess (nothing here can reach the bus from
userspace; the modesetting driver is told which node to open in xorg.conf), so
that branch is not taken and libdrm's include directory never reaches the
compiler.  The build then fails in hw/xfree86/dri2 on

    xf86drm.h:40:10: fatal error: drm.h: No such file or directory

because <drm.h> lives in ${includedir}/libdrm, which is what LIBDRM_CFLAGS
names.  The modesetting driver would fail the same way.

So add them in the other branch too, when libdrm is enabled.  A build with
libpciaccess is unaffected.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1862,6 +1862,16 @@
 		if test "x$INT10MODULE" = xyes && test "x$INT10" != xstub; then
 			AC_MSG_ERROR([Cannot build int10 without libpciaccess])
 		fi
+		dnl libdrm's flags are added above only along with libpciaccess,
+		dnl on the assumption that a server which talks to a display
+		dnl manager also enumerates the bus.  A server built without bus
+		dnl enumeration still needs them: hw/xfree86/dri2 and the
+		dnl modesetting driver include <xf86drm.h>, which includes
+		dnl <drm.h> from libdrm's own include directory.
+		if test "x$DRM" = xyes; then
+			XORG_SYS_LIBS="$XORG_SYS_LIBS $LIBDRM_LIBS"
+			XORG_CFLAGS="$XORG_CFLAGS $LIBDRM_CFLAGS"
+		fi
 	fi
 	AC_MSG_RESULT([$PCI])
 
